  "title": "React function and class components JSX props and events",
  "status": "source-backed-scope-complete",
  "concepts": [
    "Components package rendering logic into reusable units; composition nests small components to build larger interfaces.",
    "Function components receive one props object and return React nodes. Class components remain supported but functions are recommended for new code.",
    "JSX is a JavaScript syntax extension that describes elements. JavaScript expressions enter JSX through braces, while attributes use JSX-specific naming and value rules.",
    "Props are parent-to-child inputs and can carry any JavaScript value. They are read-only inputs; defaults, children, and explicit forwarding shape component interfaces.",
    "JavaScript control flow chooses which JSX to return. Conditional rendering and list rendering are expressions and mappings over ordinary data.",
    "An event handler is a function passed for React to call after an interaction. Calling it during render is different from passing the function reference.",
    "Component composition and callback props allow a parent to provide behavior while a child owns presentation; event propagation can be stopped or allowed to continue."
  ],
